  "releaseNotes": "- Postgres: the connection string is now built with NpgsqlConnectionStringBuilder instead of\n\t\t  being joined together by hand, so a database password containing a semicolon, a quote or\n\t\t  leading or trailing spaces reaches Postgres unchanged. A semicolon previously split the\n\t\t  password, and opening the connection failed with \"Couldn't set ...;timezone\".\n\t\t- Adds a direct reference to System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs 10.0.13, replacing the 9.0.18\n\t\t  that Microsoft.Data.SqlClient 7.1.1 brings in (CVE-2026-84008, CVE-2026-70162).\n\t\t- Dependency floors raised since 3.240.27: LogicMonitor.Api 3.240.97, Microsoft.Data.SqlClient\n\t\t  7.1.1, PanoramicData.Mapper 10.0.52 and PanoramicData.NCalcExtensions 6.1.45. A consumer that\n\t\t  pins any of these lower must raise its pin, or restore fails with a downgrade error.\n\t\t- Tests: back on VSTest, since xUnit v2 has no Microsoft Testing Platform entry point and no\n\t\t  tests were being discovered.",
